  "behavior": [
    "The preview, injected-request admission, local approval and WalletConnect signing use one typed-data parser. Mobile forwarding revalidates the same contract before transport.",
    "Boolean fields must be actual booleans. The string false can no longer be displayed as false while ethers encodes true. Strings, bytes, literal addresses and integers are checked before ethers range/digest validation.",
    "primaryType must match the encoder root. Message structs and arrays are checked recursively; missing and unsigned extra fields are rejected. A declared EIP712Domain schema must match the canonical schema ethers actually signs instead of being silently deleted.",
    "Unsupported legacy v1 and v3 arrays are rejected before key access or mobile forwarding. Object and JSON-string EIP-712 payloads produce the same validated intent; inputs are not mutated.",
    "Malformed typed data has no Approve or Sign anyway action in the signing screen. Valid typed data uses the existing explicit approval path and complete raw request.",
    "The UI unwraps Vue reactive arrays before the shared parser copies RPC data. This preserves strict backend validation while allowing valid object payloads in the actual store.",
    "WalletConnect typed-data domain.chainId, when present, must equal the request chain before key export. Broader session/network authorization is not implied."
  ],
