  "compatibilityLimits": [
    "Boolean strings and numeric booleans are rejected, even if a caller previously relied on library coercion. Callers must send actual JSON booleans.",
    "EIP712Domain may be omitted for existing ethers-compatible callers. When supplied, only ethers canonical field types/order are accepted; alternate declared order is conservatively rejected rather than replaced.",
    "Legacy eth_signTypedData_v1 and legacy array-shaped eth_signTypedData payloads are unsupported. The unversioned method accepts the existing EIP-712 object contract only; it is not claimed as legacy V1 support.",
    "Cyclic/recursive type graphs rejected by ethers remain unsupported. V4 arrays are supported within encoder constraints. No complete EIP-712 implementation/conformance claim is made.",
    "Addresses must be literal valid EVM addresses, bytes complete hex, integer numbers safe or exact decimal/hex strings; ENS and implicit primitive coercions are unsupported. Struct/value validation is bounded at 10,000 visits and depth 64.",
    "WalletConnect queue identity, concurrent approvals, session authorization/provider context and its separate signing screen remain open. This checkpoint only aligns its typed-data parsing and domain-chain comparison.",
